        <div class="research-entry-details">
          <p>
            <strong>Description:</strong>{" "}
            Conventional wood-chip quality assessment relies heavily on
            periodic sampling and offline measurements. Wood-Chip Monitor
            moves this process closer to real-time operations through a
            portable NVIDIA Jetson and TensorRT platform that combines dense
            chip detection, physical size estimation, size-distribution
            monitoring, oversize alerts, and image-based moisture assessment.
            A local dashboard converts the model outputs into rolling
            statistics, configurable quality rules, event records, and live
            visual feedback for operators.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Outcome:</strong>{" "}
            The project translates research models into a complete edge-AI
            prototype spanning image acquisition, accelerated inference,
            physical measurement, quality analytics, backend services, and an
            operator-facing interface. The geometry engine achieved an mAR50
            of 95% with a reported size-distribution error of KL = 0.04, while
            the lightweight moisture engine achieved 91% classification
            accuracy.
          </p>

